identifier: kgmicrobe.ingredient:jcm480_preaddition_basal_preparation
preferred_term: JCM 480 pre-addition basal preparation
ingredient_type: STOCK_SOLUTION
mapping_status: MAPPED
ontology_mapping:
  ontology_id: kgmicrobe.ingredient:jcm480_preaddition_basal_preparation
  ontology_label: JCM 480 pre-addition basal preparation
  ontology_source: kgmicrobe.ingredient
  mapping_quality: FALLBACK_REGISTRY
  evidence:
  - evidence_type: CURATOR_JUDGMENT
    source: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=480; https://togomedium.org/medium/M481
    notes: 'JCM480 prepares a basal material separately from phosphate solution and
      later bicarbonate/reductant/carbon-source additions. Source-listed trace vitamins
      remain a basal ingredient. Source transcription basis (literal input amounts,
      not calculated stock concentrations): distilled water: 900 ml; MgSO4·7H2O: 0.5
      g; Yeast extract: 0.5 g; NaCl: 2.25 g; CaCl2·2H2O: 0.25 g; NH4Cl: 0.5 g; Resazurin:
      1 mg; Casitone (BD-Difco): 0.5 g; Trace vitamins (see Medium [M190]): 10 ml;
      Trace element solution (see below): 1 ml; Se/W solution (see Medium [M312]):
      1 ml. No batch-to-final-volume conversion is made. Handling atmosphere is not
      listed as a material part; pH reagents are source inputs, without an assertion
      of unchanged molecular species after pH adjustment. Nested formulations remain
      source-qualified named parts where exact composition/owner identity is not established.
      No verified exact eligible ontology term or existing whole-preparation owner
      was established by the bounded source/owner review. This self-registry mapping
      represents the preparation, not its individual constituents.'
